Chapter: Pr87ArmB
  cites Foreword chapter Console

 PR 87's EXECUTION datum, which the Cobblestone lane asked for: every one
 of their seven arms was compiled to IR text, not run. This is their arm
 B -- the one that COMPILES -- given a base case so it terminates, and
 executed on the zig arm.

 Arm B is a FULL-arity self tail call whose result happens to be a
 function. It is not the shape PR 87 worried about, and it is the shape
 PR 87's own reproducer had, which is why that reproducer compiled and
 could not reproduce.

 `should-tco` will fire on it: one parameter, a tail position, and
 `is-self-call` matches the name. So the pass rewrites it as a loop and
 the returned closure must still be the right one.

 PREDICTION: 5. `gb 3` counts down to `gb 0`, which answers the identity
 lambda, and applying that to 5 gives 5. A wrong answer here would say
 the TCO rewrite loses the closure the last frame built.

Section: Functions

  gb : Integer -> (Integer -> Integer)
  gb (x) = if x <= 0 then (\y -> y) else gb (x - 1)

Section: Entry

  opening : [Console] Nothing
  opening = act
   print-line-uni (show ((gb 3) 5))
  end
